{
  "dom_id": "step-q34957",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Express $\\sqrt{\\frac{2z}{z-1}}\\,$ without radicals in the denominator.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the quotient rule and put the numerator and denominator under separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{2z}{z-1}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2z}}{\\sqrt{z-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the radical $\\sqrt{z-1}$ from the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{z-1}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2z}}{\\sqrt{z-1}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2z}}{\\sqrt{z-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{z-1}}{\\sqrt{z-1}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2z}\\cdot \\sqrt{z-1}}{\\sqrt{z-1}\\cdot \\sqrt{z-1}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2z(z-1)}}{{(\\sqrt{z-1})}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2z(z-1)}}{z-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
